    "reasoning": "All twelve answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-32092: the determinant is 5-k; nonintersecting lines require equal slopes, so k=5 and the determinant is zero. q-73566: det(A)=2, so A is invertible, the lines intersect uniquely, and Ax=0 has the zero solution; only II is true. q-71882: A lies on the circle's boundary, while B and C are interior; I and III are true. q-36432: A is interior, while B and C are boundary points; I and II are true. q-105334: P has squared radius 4, so it is excluded from A but belongs to its boundary; Q has squared radius 8 and is interior. q-105336: P gives 4x²+9y²=72 and belongs to A but not its boundary; Q gives 36 and is a boundary point, not interior. For the motion questions, acceleration satisfies a=v dv/dx=d(v²/2)/dx. q-122313 requires negative acceleration toward the origin. q-107998 has a=4x². q-122339 integrates to v²=x²/16+4 and requires the negative root. q-122337 integrates to v²=2(e^(x-3)+1) and requires the positive root. q-122316 integrates (1+x)² dx=dt and uses x(0)=0. q-122351 first gives v=4(x+1)^(1/4), then integration with x(0)=0 gives x=(3t+1)^(4/3)-1. No grade evidence was supplied; confirmation uses the quoted worked solutions.",
